{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And also.</b> They are the firstborn. Though they are holy, as written: \"Sanctify to me every firstborn\" (above, Exodus 13:2), they shall add to sanctify themselves further in their thought." "<b>And the meaning of \"who draw near to YHWH.\"</b> That they are at the edge of the boundary. Or its meaning is that they offered burnt offerings on the altar that Moses built at the weakening of Amalek; they too shall offer on the altar of the covenant that Moses built and established at the foot of the mountain, where all Israel stood to hear the voice of HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:59.424555093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}